{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01Rey2MGb5aQnGRGK2NrSDPC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Looking at the parsing, the rate \"00550\" with PIC 9(3)V9(2) should be interpreted as 005.50 (5.50%). The monthly rate should be 5.50/1200 = 0.00458333.\n\nFor loan 5000 at 0.458333% monthly for 12 months:\n- Monthly payment = 5000 * 0.00458333 / (1 - 1.00458333^-12) = 428.04\n\nBut expected shows 400. Let me check if the example is showing a specific scenario or if there's another interpretation. Actually, looking more carefully at the expected output:\n- Payment = 400.00\n- Interest = 22.92 (which is 5000 * 0.004583 = 22.92) ✓\n- Principal = 377.08 (400 - 22.92 = 377.08) ✓\n- Remaining = 4622.92 (5000 - 377.08 = 4622.92) ✓\n\nSo if payment is 400, the math works. But annuity formula would give ~428 for 12 months. Maybe the example uses a different calculation approach or different parameters.\n\nLooking again at the input - maybe the LOAN_AMOUNT after deducting DOWN_PAYMENT?\n- Loan = 5000, Down = 3500, Net Loan = 1500? No, that doesn't fit either.\n\nActually, looking at the raw numbers in the issue description example again - the values in the example output may just be illustrative. Let me verify my calculation is correct with proper annuity formula and see if the program is working correctly.\n\nThe issue I see is that the interest (2291.66) is way too high. 5000 * 5.5 / 1200 = 22.92, not 2291.66. So the rate is being interpreted incorrectly. The rate is coming as 550 (integer part) instead of 5.50."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":393,"cache_read_input_tokens":25049,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":393,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c356a6e-3a6b-4a08-ac27-53910b574c21","uuid":"35cd9515-c691-48fb-b04d-f6010ab82fe3"}
